/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Transforms Transforms
 * @ingroup DspCore
 * @brief Configured block Fourier transforms and their inverse operations.
 *
 * DFT<Real> is the O(N^2) direct reference transform and accepts every
 * nonzero configured size. FFT<Real> is an O(N log N) radix-2 transform and
 * accepts only powers of two. Both consume caller-owned Processing::SampleBlock
 * views of Foundation::Math::Complex<Real>, offer Forward and Inverse, and
 * include ForwardReal for real input. Forward is unnormalised; Inverse applies
 * 1/N, so a successful inverse of a successful forward transform reconstructs
 * the input within floating-point error.
 *
 * Configure allocates the transform workspace. Calls after Configure perform
 * no allocation, require valid input/output views exactly N elements long,
 * validate finite values and leave the output unchanged on failure. The
 * workspace makes exact input/output aliasing safe. These are block transforms:
 * they do not own a clock, stream, FIFO, hop size, window, or overlap-add
 * policy. A streaming analysis/synthesis adaptor is a separate future API.
 */
